      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ONELOOK (5) was returning from a layoff last start when she made up plenty of ground to finish third a week-and-a-half ago over 1690m at Shepparton. Steps up a level but she is fitter and good enough to cope. MY ROCKING HORSE (2) was in the money on debut two runs ago then went well again last time over 2190m at Shepparton, finishing 5 metres from the winner in second. A nice draw on the front line should ensure a cosy run. Taking on a better line-up this time but she has the ability to mix it with them. LA CANTATRICE (7) comes right into contention after scoring last start by a neck at Ballarat over 2200m. OZZIE TART (4) must be respected after scoring last start by 2 metres at Launceston over 1680m.",
